# Wrap up

The Penang cellar is the "second-line leader" in good industry – second-tier than the bottom, less profitable than the old cellar pool, but under-pricing brands, falling industry ranking, and a ceiling for state corporate governance. The 13-fold PE+5.8% rate currently provides a "not much to lose" security cushion, but the industry’s no stop, management is about to change, and the price of the cellar is still not settled, which means that "favourable" may not be cheap enough.

In the words of Yongping: This is a "good but not great" business, which can be bought at a good price, but not a "sleeping safe" warehouse.

